    "created_at": "2016-10-18T16:49:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-18T16:49:42Z",
    "body": "So, what do people think of this? To recap, issues like #1811 and #1087 show that web developers and implementers are generally confused by how datalists should behave and display. The idea is for the spec to provide some \"should\" UI guidance, and hope that browser converge on that. The particular UI guidance is:\n- Display both label and value\n- Search on both label and value\n- Search using substring matching\n\nThe current browser landscape (which appears to have changed since #1087) is:\n- Blink:\n  - Displays both label and value\n  - Searches both label and value\n  - Searches using substring matching\n- Edge:\n  - Displays label only\n  - Searches on value only\n  - Searches using prefix matching\n- Gecko:\n  - Displays label only\n  - Searches on label only\n  - Searches using substring matching\n- WebKit:\n  - does not implement datalist as far as I can tell\n\nSo this spec guidance matches Blink's behavior, which is a union of the Edge and Gecko behavior and is IMO the most user-friendly.\n\nPinging @travisleithead @jessi3py @cdumez for their thoughts. I'm interested in both whether you think adding this guidance to the spec is a good idea, and separately, whether you think your browsers are interested in updating to follow it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
